WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.270
Our club's agent had ten tools.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.820
It only needed two of them.

3
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.850
Then a tampered web page tricked it into

4
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:13.130
using a third: it messaged every parent.

5
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.020
Today: give an AI agent only the tools it

6
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.240
needs, and make it ask before it acts.

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.060
An AI agent is a model that can

8
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.980
use tools: the timetable, the

9
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.720
library, reminders, messages.

10
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.080
The model decides which tool to call.

11
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.200
And as you saw last lesson,

12
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.400
the model can be tricked.

13
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.120
Tools come in two kinds.

14
00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.030
Reading tools look things up: at worst, a

15
00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.490
trick makes them leak something.

16
00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.090
Acting tools change the world: they

17
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.090
send, delete, pay or post, and a

18
00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.710
trick can turn them against you.

19
00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.810
That's why we use least privilege.

20
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.140
Give an agent the fewest tools its

21
00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.520
job needs, reading before acting,

22
00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.140
for the shortest time.

23
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.410
Everything it holds is its blast radius:

24
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.510
all that an attack could reach.

25
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.420
Quick check!

26
00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:17.930
An agent plans tomorrow's homework from

27
00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.070
the timetable and the library.

28
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.990
Which tools should it get?

29
00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.800
Timetable and library only.

30
00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.610
With no acting tool, a tampered

31
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.670
result can make it read or talk,

32
00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.210
but it can't do anything.

33
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.590
Its blast radius is close to zero.

34
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.920
Now write it down as an

35
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.420
allow-list, in code.

36
00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.020
For each task, list the tools it may use.

37
00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.870
Before any tool runs, code checks the

38
00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.350
list, and anything else is refused,

39
00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.270
whatever the model asked for.

40
00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.530
Some tasks really do need an acting

41
00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.450
tool, like sending a reminder.

42
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.910
Then add a second rule: an acting tool

43
00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:04.690
runs only after a person says yes.

44
00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.960
And that yes is checked in code,

45
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.660
never left to the model.

46
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.000
In the app, pick a job and

47
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:13.900
grant some tools.

48
00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.850
Then run the set of tampered results

49
00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.670
and count the harmful actions.

50
00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.410
Grant only the timetable

51
00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.130
and library: zero.

52
00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.270
Add send message, and run it again.

53
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.240
Your turn.

54
00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.520
The reminder task holds the send tool.

55
00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.470
A tampered result asks it to message

56
00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.910
everyone, and nobody said yes.

57
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.940
What does the check return?

58
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.320
Ask first: the tool is

59
00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.420
allowed, but nobody said yes.

60
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.700
Remember: reading tools can leak,

61
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.340
and acting tools can be turned.

62
00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.360
Give the fewest tools, check an

63
00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.660
allow-list in code, and need a

64
00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.320
person's yes before anything acts.

65
00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.860
Try it tomorrow: pick one assistant

66
00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.160
or app on your phone, or on a

67
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.420
family phone with its owner.

68
00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.490
List what it can do, and mark each

69
00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.650
power as reading or acting.

70
00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.650
Switch off one acting

71
00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.910
power it doesn't need.
